## CI/CD Workflow Patterns

### Standard CI Pipeline

```yaml
name: Python CI

on:
  push:
    branches: [main, feature/**]
  pull_request:
    branches: [main]

jobs:
  quality:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
      - uses: astral-sh/setup-uv@v3
        with:
          enable-cache: true
      - run: uv sync --group dev
      - run: uv run ruff check .
      - run: uv run ruff format --check .

  test:
    needs: quality
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
      - uses: astral-sh/setup-uv@v3
      - run: uv sync --group dev
      - run: uv run pytest -m "not internet and not slow and not ollama" --junitxml=test-results.xml --cov=src --cov-report=xml
      - uses: actions/upload-artifact@v4
        if: always()
        with:
          name: test-results
          path: test-results.xml
```

### Pre-Quality Gate Checklist

```bash
# Run all quality checks before declaring ready
uv run ruff check .
uv run ruff format --check .
uv run pytest -m "not internet and not slow and not ollama" --cov=src --cov-fail-under=80
```

## Markers and Test Categories

### Marker Configuration

The project uses pytest markers to categorize tests:

| Marker | Purpose | Default | CI Behaviour |
|--------|---------|---------|--------------|
| `slow` | Tests >5 seconds | Skipped | Skipped |
| `internet` | Network-dependent | Skipped | Skipped |
| `ollama` | Requires local Ollama | Skipped | Skipped |
| `docker` | Requires Docker stack | Skipped | Skipped |
| `fts5` | Requires SQLite FTS5 | Included | Included |
| `ci_setup` | CI/CD configuration | Included | Included |

### Marker Verification

```bash
# Verify all tests have correct markers
uv run pytest --co -q  # list all test names with markers

# Run only the CI subset
uv run pytest -m "not internet and not slow and not ollama"
```

## Quality Gate Enforcement

### Pre-Merge Gate Steps

```bash
# Step 1: Linting and formatting
uv run ruff check .
if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { throw "Linting failed" }

uv run ruff format --check .
if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { throw "Formatting failed" }

# Step 2: Tests with coverage
uv run pytest -m "not internet and not slow and not ollama" --cov=src --cov-fail-under=80 --junitxml=test-results.xml
if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { throw "Tests failed or coverage below 80%" }

# Step 3: Type checking if configured
# uv run mypy src/ --strict

# Step 4: Security check
# uv run bandit -r src/ -q
```

### Post-Merge Verification

```bash
# Verify CI pipeline passes on target branch
gh run list --workflow "Python CI" --limit 1 --branch main --json conclusion
```

## Code Complete Verification Checklist

### Construction Quality Audit

- [ ] All functions have appropriate error handling — no bare `except:` clauses
- [ ] Input validation at all trust boundaries (API, file loading, user input)
- [ ] Assertions document critical preconditions and postconditions
- [ ] No deeply nested conditionals (max 3 levels; flag deeper for refactoring)
- [ ] All paths have explicit returns
- [ ] No commented-out code
- [ ] TODO comments reference a task/story ID or are sufficiently described
- [ ] No magic numbers — all constants named
- [ ] String formatting is consistent (f-strings preferred)
- [ ] No `print()` statements (use logger)
- [ ] Imports are clean — no unused, no wildcard, grouped correctly

### Test Quality Audit

- [ ] Each test has a business-purpose docstring per test-documentation standard
- [ ] Tests are organized in classes mapping to components
- [ ] Each class has a docstring describing scope
- [ ] Tests use appropriate markers (`slow`, `internet`, `ollama`, etc.)
- [ ] No test depends on another test's state (isolated)
- [ ] Test names describe the scenario, not just the function
- [ ] Edge cases are tested alongside happy path
- [ ] Mocked services are used for external dependencies

## Git Handover Workflow

### 1. Receiving Code Refactorer Handover

When receiving handover from Code Refactorer:

```bash
# Check handover notes
cat tmp/handover/STORY-XXX-refactorer-guardian-handover.md

# Run quality assessment
uv run ruff check src/ --statistics
uv run ruff format --check src/
uv run pytest -m "not internet and not slow and not ollama" --cov=src
```

### 2. Quality Assessment

```bash
# Full quality audit
echo "STORY-XXX Quality Assessment:
- Linting Status: [pass/fail + counts]
- Formatting Status: [pass/fail]
- Test Results: [pass/fail + counts]
- Coverage: [percentage %]
- Security Scan: [pass/fail]
- Quality Verdict: [PASS/FAIL/CONDITIONAL]
- Issues Found: [list issues]" > tmp/handover/STORY-XXX-quality-assessment-report.md
```

### 3. Quality Handover

```bash
# Report quality status to DDD Code Architect and Code Refactorer
echo "STORY-XXX quality handover:
- Overall Verdict: [PASS/FAIL]
- Critical Issues: [list]
- Blocking Items: [list]
- Recommendations: [improvements]" > tmp/handover/STORY-XXX-guardian-handover.md
```

## Quality Gates

### CI/CD Pipeline Checklist

- [ ] CI workflows defined for push and PR
- [ ] Linting step runs `ruff check` on all Python files
- [ ] Formatting step runs `ruff format --check`
- [ ] Test step runs with correct marker exclusions
- [ ] Coverage threshold enforced (≥80%)
- [ ] Test results uploaded as artifacts
- [ ] Pipeline completes in under 10 minutes
- [ ] Dependencies are cached for faster runs

### Quality Gate Checklist

- [ ] All linting checks pass
- [ ] All formatting checks pass
- [ ] All tests pass (excluding skipped markers)
- [ ] Coverage meets threshold
- [ ] No flaky tests identified
- [ ] Security scan clean
- [ ] Code Complete construction quality verified
- [ ] Technical debt items registered for identified issues
- [ ] Quality assessment documented
- [ ] Handover completed

## Integration with Other Roles

### DDD Code Architect

- **Coverage Reporting**: Share coverage reports for domain code
- **Quality Metrics**: Report quality per bounded context
- **Lint Rule Feedback**: Suggest rule adjustments for domain-specific patterns

### Code Refactorer

- **Pre-Refactoring Baseline**: Capture quality metrics before refactoring starts
- **Post-Refactoring Verification**: Confirm refactoring didn't reduce quality
- **Flaky Test Resolution**: Flag tests that fail intermittently during refactoring

### Software Architect

- **Linting Workflow Ownership**: Support Software Architect's linting workflow (the single source of truth)
- **Pipeline Approval**: Sign off on CI/CD changes
- **Quality Standards**: Enforce Software Architect's quality standards automatically in CI

### Software Developer

- **Pre-Commit Feedback**: Provide clear error messages when checks fail
- **Developer Experience**: Keep pipelines fast so developers run them locally too

